some fans thought it would never happen  but netflix is finally bringing the  sandman to live action who is trusted to  bring the enigmatic dream to life and  who rounds out the rest of this all-star  cast watch this before you see the  sandman  netflix's the sandman is set to premiere  on august 5th 2022 considering that the  author himself once claimed to have  spent 30 years battling against bad  adaptations the fact that this series is  so close to release is incredibly  encouraging the series originally  entered post-production on july 23 2021  and then again on april 17th 2022 it's  unclear exactly why there are currently  two separate periods of post-production  but it was likely to make sure the  finished show will truly bring to life  neil gaiman's vision the average time it  takes for a feature-length film to go  from raw footage to the final product is  around six months to a year this  includes editing sound mixing color  correction visual effects and a host of  other processes that need to be  completed before the project's release  because the total run time of netflix is  the sandman will undoubtedly be much  longer than the average film it could  explain why there were two separate  phases in any case we can't wait to see  the dream finally make it to tv screens  on august 5th  tom sturridge takes on the role of dream  a powerful figure also known as morpheus  or the sandman dream is one of the seven  endless a family of beings who represent  different aspects of the universe he's  an immensely powerful character who  rules over a kingdom known as the  dreaming death as family  desire  destiny  despair though sturge will serve as the  lead of the series he's just one of many  familiar faces you'll see in the massive  ensemble cast of the sandman one of the  prominent roles in the series belongs to  kirby howell baptist who plays death in  the series she's most well known for her  roles in killing eve and the good place  then there's jenna coleman who plays  johanna constantine who in the comics is  the great great great grandmother of  john constantine the series will reunite  game of thrones alumni charles dance and  gwendolyn christie dance takes over the  role of occultist roderick burgess while  christy inhabits the character of  lucifer morningstar and the legendary  mark hamill provides the voice of mervin  pumpkinhead the list of actors is so  long it's hard to get into them all but  all told the cast of the sandman is  filled from top to bottom with some of  the most talented and well-known actors  out there  fans will be overjoyed to hear that  these beloved characters are in such  experienced hands  the story of netflix is the sandman will  follow the plot of neil gaiman's  original comic series at the beginning  of the story dream is captured by the  occultist roderick burgess and is held  captive for over 70 years dream's  lengthy absence wreaks havoc across the  universe as a whole and when he finally  escapes he is forced to set out on a  lengthy journey to restore order and fix  his past mistakes forgive me messiah the  palace the realm  they are not as you left them gaming  also clarified that the first 10  episodes of the series will cover the  first two volumes of the comic preludes  and nocturnes and the doll's house the  first volume follows dream as he  reacquires the magical tools that were  stolen from him during his imprisonment  the second volume is chiefly concerned  with a serial killer convention subtle  machinations from dream's sibling desire  and the emergence of a dream vortex  which could spell doom for sandman's  kingdom beyond these small details about  the plot information about the series  itself remains sparse though the  recently released trailer gives us a few  pretty significant clues about what to  expect in netflix's the sandman  the trailer for the sandman focuses  heavily on dream and his kingdom of the  dreaming from what we see in the trailer  it seems like dream is released from his  occult prison when two police officers  shoot at him and shatter the glass walls  that surround him from there we watch  him return to his kingdom and discover  that the dreaming has turned into a  decayed ruin in his absence we get a  brief glimpse of death dreams loyal  sister as well as the villainous john d  the latter of whom is holding a ruby  that fans will recognize as very  important to the plot of the original  comic finally we get a brief but  chilling shot of a man with bleeding  eyes who may be the corinthian a  malevolent nightmare who escaped the  dreaming during his master's absence  even though this first trailer is only a  teaser for what's to come we are still  able to extract a surprising amount of  story from it in any case the trailer is  certain to get plenty of fans excited  for the upcoming series especially since  it's taken so long to see this project  actually completed  the star studded sandman castles could  even rival denis villeneuve's dune in  terms of sheer celebrity wattage however  it took some time before the names  involved in the project were revealed to  the world when they were they arrived in  a gigantic batch that had the internet  chattering for better or for worse neil  gaiman wrote the casting announcements  as well as a brief description of the  characters and why the chosen actors  were right for the roles introducing  patent oswalt as matthew the raven  gaiman disclosed an interesting detail  about the actors casting explaining how  the sandman team searched for someone  who had the voice acting abilities to  make the audience invested in such a  peculiar character and was also a fan of  the comic book series gaiman revealed  patton was the first person we asked and  the first person we cast the day before  we pitched the sandman to netflix  considering the sandman and lucifer are  both netflix properties featuring the  same character many fans presumed that  tom ellis would play the devilishly  dapper lord of hell in dream's story  however when the casting news dropped it  was revealed that game of thrones actor  gwendolyn christie had been cast as  lucifer instead many people didn't  understand why ellis didn't get the role  since he was exceptionally popular as  the character and already had an  established fan base this is especially  true considering that the netflix  lucifer series is based on the comic by  the same name which was a direct  spin-off of the sandman answering these  fan questions on tumblr neil gaiman  addressed the reasons for ellis's  absence from the series he replied the  theology and cosmogeny of netflix's  lucifer is a long way from sandman's  it's inspired by sandman but you can't  easily retrofit the lucifer version to  get back to sandman if you see what i  mean it seemed easier and more fun to  have the sandman version of lucifer be  well much closer to the sandman version  of lucifer gaiman once again discussed  the issue on his twitter account  explaining how ellis version of the  character was too different by the end  of the show and far more lovable than  the sandman iteration in other words  christie's lucifer isn't meant to be  very nice or laughable those who've read  the sandman know the series plays an  important role in the overall dc  universe it isn't uncommon to see dream  and the others interacting with  characters such as batman or john  constantine constantine appears early on  in the sandman comic series when he  helps dream reclaim his magical pouch of  dreams and shortly after escaping  burgess's imprisonment many fans  expected to see the character appearing  in the series perhaps even with matt  ryan reprising his role as the  chainsmoking hellblazer however when the  cast was announced jenna coleman was  revealed to be portraying johanna  constantine with no mention of jon in  sight considering that coleman's  character appears in the sandman trailer  adapting a scene from the comics that  starred jon the more rowdy part of the  internet got into a tangle believing  that the character had been gender  swapped for the sandman however that  simply isn't true johanna was a  character created by neil gaiman as a  tribute and included in the original  sandman comics in the comics she's an  ancestor of jon and has her own  intriguing backstory in all likelihood  netflix also probably wasn't able to  secure the rights to use john  constantine in this series since the  characters tied up in other dc projects  in various stages of production we'll  have to wait and see just how johanna  fits in with the series  before desire was even cast there had  been many suggestions about who could  play dream's rebellious sibling on  screen many fans drew up their dream  lists of potential actors for this  pivotal part and some performers decided  to put their names in the mix as well  while twitter might be a platform that's  notorious for feeding the outrage  machine it can also open doors and  connect people in positive ways just ask  mason alexander park as revealed by neil  gaiman in the cast announcements for the  sandman park reached out through twitter  in the early stages of the casting  process they certainly must have  impressed gaiman and the casting agents  since park got the part  the sandman has been a long time in the  making much like its characters it has  gone through various shapes and forms  before finally settling on a netflix  series as soon as the decision was made  on what it would be the casting process  for the show became one of the most  important parts of the production  process however this wasn't a cut and  dry case of approaching the big name  actors they had in mind and auditioning  for the rest boyd holbrook revealed to  collider that he had to go through a  lengthy auditioning process to secure  the role of the corinthian he explained  i read the script and they were really  adamant about everyone auditioning so i  went in and then i didn't hear anything  until probably like september or  something like that anyways it was a  long process and the conversation just  started and they wanted to tape again  and they wanted me to meet with neil and  talk about just how the show was going  to be done  boyd holbrook wasn't the only one who  had to endure a long auditioning process  tom sturridge is another cast member who  didn't walk into the room and get  offered the role on the spot while  sturge might have an impressive list of  credits having appeared in the hollow  crown sweetbitter and mary shelley he  still had a long hard road to travel  before being cast in the sandman while  many actors wanted the role of dream  there were two legitimate contenders  that sturge had to battle for the part  according to collider palldark and  american gods actor tom york and colin  morgan who appeared in merlin and  belfast were tested for the role and  were given serious consideration since  york had worked on a previous neil  gaiman adaptation his fellow candidates  for the part of dream must have been  sweating that he'd be the front runner  fortunately for sturge he impressed the  right people and got the role in the end  you know the same way  he's a fairy story eddie  he's no fairy story he's back  while the sandman is positioned as a  dark fantasy series it does feature many  thought-provoking themes especially  about the meaning of life and death  anyone who has read the comics can  attest to this for example in the  sandman number 13 dream and an immortal  man known as hob meet up once every  hundred years to discuss humanity death  and everything in between it's a  thought-provoking series of  conversations that makes the reader  question many aspects of their existence  during a tour to discuss his career  gaiman revealed to the audience that  episode 6 of the sandman made him cry he  explained that even though he had  written the scene and knew what was  going to happen it hit him hard when he  saw it replayed in live action perhaps  the characters will dive deeper into the  themes that will have us all  experiencing an existential crisis after  watching the show the 2020 pandemic was  a strange time not only was there a lot  of uncertainty around everything  happening in the world but it also  caused millions of people to spend more  time at home some decided to bake banana  bread and experiment on tick tock while  others developed an unhealthy obsession  with netflix's tiger king series the  production of the sandman was also  impacted by the pandemic due to the  travel bans and restrictions on  in-person interactions netflix pushed  development timelines and had everyone  wondering what would happen next  neil gaiman revealed to entertainment  weekly that warner brothers paid tom  sturridge to not take another role and  stay on standby even though it wasn't  certain he would be cast as dream  additionally netflix decided to make use  of the extra time and encouraged the  casting team to look at every single  audition received gaiman explained that  he looked at over 1  500 auditions for dream before the  decision to cast sturridge was finally  made though fans may have wanted the  series to arrive sooner it seems like  this casting was a dream come true  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the sandman are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

